        "id": 13206,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-28T15:58:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Just finished a game against Voss with the heroes near full strength.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>GI Bunker started with Ammo Drop</p><p>Young Legacy started with Inspiring Prescence</p><p>Mr. Fixer started with Dual Crowbars</p><p>Ra played Imbued Fire</p><p>Absolute Zero neutered a Forced Deployment with Fueled Freeze</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Neither ship came out.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Realm of Discord had little negative effect. Positive Energy didn't help the minions enough to keep them alive. Time Crawls only slowed me down a little. Ethereal Bubbles got one-shot by the second hit from Dual Crowbars. Time Flies was fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Bunker had a hand full of cards but never got to take advantage of Gatling Gun or Omnicannon because of Time Crawls. Both of them got played when Time Flies came out, but I won the game a couple hero turns later. Bunker's removal of Voss' DR meant I could leave one minion out and just pound Voss on his front side. I actually had to leave two minions out so that Mr. Fixer would have a first target with his Dual Crowbars so he could hit Voss as the second target.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Imbued Fire meant Absolute Zero couldn't heal himself after the first round, making Thermal Shockwave less useful, but two Impaling Structures were quite nice.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:56.520Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
